'<tool_call edit> path=/work/run/out/manifest.json (110 chars) [{"newText": " \"permissions\": [\n \"scripting\"\n ],", "oldText": " \"content_security_policy\": {}"}]
The `popup.js` uses `chrome.runtime.getBackgroundPage`. This is gone in MV3.
It does:
```javascript
chrome.runtime.getBackgroundPage(function(bgPage) {
      msg = bgPage.getMsg();
      // ...
});
```
And `service_worker.js` has:
```javascript
function getMsg(){
  return msg;
}
```
And it has a global variable `msg` that is updated when a message is received from `content.js`.

To fix this, I should use `chrome.runtime.sendMessa'

